comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T16:09:55.029Z",pi-agent,"Coverage before (origin/main, measured with npm run coverage):\n\n- index.ts lines 84.24 / branches 81.91 / functions 82.95\n- statements track lines under V8 (same 84.24)\n- uncovered regions classified as:\n  - real untested behaviour: httpsGet/httpsPost/httpsPut, fetchAllJiraIssues, createPmItem, live import/export/jira-sync/validate/preflight/onWrite, readPmItems error envelopes, non-atomic import\n  - error/edge paths: empty --map/--status-map names, unknown priority fallback, ADF non-text nodes, invalid diagnose URL, SDK import failure cache poison, settings unreadable, HTTP 401/404/timeout\n  - not dead: all of the above are reachable; none deleted; no c8 ignore\n\nCoverage after:\n\n- index.ts lines 100.00 / branches 100.00 / functions 100.00\n- coverageGate thresholds raised to 100/100/100\n- no behaviour deleted\n\nRed-on-revert confirmations (break, observe FAIL, restore):\n\n1. mapJiraPriority unknown-name fallback changed from return 3 to return 1\n   FAIL: AssertionError 1 !== 3 at test/coverage-unit.test.ts:70 (test \"mapJiraPriority covers critical, lowest, and unknown names\")\n\n2. parseFieldMap empty-name guard changed from throw CommandError to continue\n   FAIL: AssertionError Missing expected exception at test/coverage-unit.test.ts:88 (test \"parseFieldMap rejects empty names...\")\n\n3. handlePushOnWrite catch rethrows instead of swallowing\n   FAIL: Error: diagnose boom at test/coverage-unit.test.ts:279 via handlePushOnWrite (test \"handlePushOnWrite no-ops, swallows diagnose failures...\")\n\nProduction changes kept behaviour and only added test seams:\n- setPmSdkImporter so the process-wide SDK cache/import-failure paths are exercisable\n- handlePushOnWrite extracted so the hook swallow path is a real fail-able test\n- optionsOrEmpty extracted so falsy options bags are unit-tested without lying about harness defaults\n"
files[5]{path,scope,note}:
  dist/index.js,project,rebuilt dist
  index.ts,project,test seams and optionsOrEmpty/handlePushOnWrite extracts
  package.json,project,coverageGate thresholds 100/100/100
  test/coverage-runtime.test.ts,project,"HTTP, spawn, command, importer, exporter, and atomic resolution coverage"
  test/coverage-unit.test.ts,project,pure behavioural coverage for previously unreached branches
tests[3]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
